## If something goes wrong { #help }

??? question "I lost my admin link"
    Connect to the server again and run this; your admin links are shown again:

    ```bash
    hiddify admin
    ```

    If you run just `hiddify`, the management menu opens (update, restart, status and more).

??? question "The install failed: Installation Failed!"
    1. Run the install command once more; most of the time this fixes it.
    2. Make sure the server runs Ubuntu 26.04 or 24.04 (22.04 only as a last resort) and has no other services on it.
    3. If it still fails, ask in the [Telegram group](https://t.me/hiddify_board) or on [GitHub](https://github.com/hiddify/Hiddify-Manager/issues), and send the logs from `/opt/hiddify-manager/data/log/`.

??? question "The message only works on Ubuntu 22 and above"
    The server's Ubuntu is too old. In your server provider's panel, reinstall the system with Ubuntu 24.04 or 26.04 (Rebuild / Reinstall) and try again.

??? question "My admin link does not open"
    Make sure you copied the whole link without changes. See [the correct format of the admin link](/manager/domain-worker-cdn-and-tunneling/The-correct-format-of-admin-link/).

??? question "I cannot connect to the server"
    Check the IP and password again in your server provider's email. Follow [How to connect with SSH](/manager/installation-and-setup/How-to-connect-to-server-via-SSH/) step by step.

??? question "I don't have a server yet"
    [Installation prerequisites](/manager/installation-and-setup/Installation-prerequisites/) tells you what server to buy and from which server provider.

